<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Tepanec Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">1367 CE – 1428 CE (approx.) · capital Azcapotzalco</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dominant power of the Valley of Mexico before the Aztecs, ruled from Azcapotzalco, which the Mexica overthrew in 1428.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanecs</a> settled on the western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a>, with their capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a>, in the 13th century. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a>, who ruled from about 1367 to 1426, they expanded across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, using the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tlatelolco">Tlatelolco</a> as tributary allies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> realm was a tributary state: subject altepetl kept their rulers but owed tribute and military service. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a> conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/culhuacan">Culhuacan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xaltocan">Xaltocan</a> and in 1418 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/texcoco">Texcoco</a>, and placed relatives on several thrones, including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tlatelolco">Tlatelolco</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a> was a large city and an important slave market.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc's</a> death, his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxtla">Maxtla</a> seized power and turned on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itzcoatl">Itzcoatl</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualcoyotl">Nezahualcoyotl</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/texcoco">Texcoco</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a>, destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a> in 1428. The victors formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1367 CE – 1428 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.91%;width:1.21%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1367 CE – 1428 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Azcapotzalco</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tezozomoc, Maxtla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mesoamerican religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nahuatl</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Azcapotzalco, Tepanecs, Tepaneca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1398&amp;focus=tepanec-empire" aria-label="Tepanec Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2000 1456 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tepanec Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-ti